concept <ref refid="conceptscl_1_1feature_1_1concepts_1_1compatible__with__part__of" kindref="compound">scl::feature::concepts::compatible_with_part_of</ref> =  <ref refid="group__scl__feature__type__traits_1gabf1d9a783e2c33a3c5d23df001183a80" kindref="member">::scl::feature::is_compatible_with_part_of_v</ref>&lt;Expected, Type&gt;    </initializer>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Satisfied when <computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> is compatible with a part of <computeroutput>Expected</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> (a wrapper) is compatible with a nested layer of <computeroutput>Expected</computeroutput>, meaning <computeroutput>Expected</computeroutput> can be constructed with <computeroutput>Type</computeroutput> as its value argument.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Expected</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The target wrapper type. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Type</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The source type to check.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="keyword">using<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">W<sp/><sp/>=<sp/>wrapper&lt;int,<sp/>plain&gt;;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">using<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">WW<sp/>=<sp/>wrapper&lt;W,<sp/><sp/><sp/>plain&gt;;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">static_assert</highlight><highlight class="normal">(<sp/>compatible_with_part_of&lt;WW,<sp/>W&gt;);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">static_assert</highlight><highlight class="normal">(!compatible_with_part_of&lt;W,<sp/><sp/>WW&gt;);</highlight></codeline>
